      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Eraserhead** (1977) stands as David Lynch's breakthrough nightmare, shot in stark black-and-white over five years in Los Angeles. The film follows Henry Spencer's descent into parental horror when his deformed child won't stop crying. Lynch crafted this surrealist masterpiece while living in Philadelphia's industrial wasteland, channeling his fears of fatherhood and urban decay. The influence ripples through body horror classics like **Tetsuo: The Iron Man** (1989) and **Begotten** (1990), establishing a new vocabulary for experimental midnight cinema."
